"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L4\",[[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@7\"}]}]]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,null],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"children\":\"$La\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$Lc\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}],false]],\"m\":\"$undefined\",\"G\":[\"$d\",[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]]],\"S\":true,\"h\":null,\"s\":\"$undefined\",\"l\":\"$undefined\",\"p\":\"$undefined\",\"d\":\"$undefined\",\"b\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\ne:[]\n8:\"$We\"\nf:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"\"]\n10:I[16505,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"LessonClient\"]\n11:Tb52,# Credentials and SecureStrings\n\nHandling credentials securely is critical in automation. PowerShell provides built-in tools to work with usernames and passwords without exposing them as plain text.\n\n## Get-Credential\n\nThe `Get-Credential` cmdlet prompts for a username and password, returning a `PSCredential` object:\n\n```powershell\n$cred = Get-Credential\n$cred = Get-Credential -UserName 'DOMAIN\\Admin' -Message 'Enter admin password'\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Never hard-code passwords in scripts. Always use `Get-Credential` or retrieve credentials from a secure store.\n\n## The PSCredential Object\n\nA `PSCredential` object has two properties: `UserName` (a plain string) and `Password` (a `SecureString`). You can also construct one manually:\n\n```powershell\n$user = 'DOMAIN\\ServiceAccount'\n$pass = Read-Host -Prompt 'Password' -AsSecureString\n$cred = [PSCredential]::new($user, $pass)\n```\n\n## Working with SecureStrings\n\nA `SecureString` encrypts text in memory. You can convert a plain string to a `SecureString` using `ConvertTo-SecureString`:\n\n```powershell\n# From user input (interactive)\n$secure = Read-Host -AsSecureString\n\n# From a plain string (use only for testing, not production)\n$secure = ConvertTo-SecureString 'MyPassword' -AsPlainText -Force\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** `ConvertTo-SecureString -AsPlainText` is useful for testing but defeats the purpose of a SecureString. In production, always get passwords from interactive prompts or secure stores.\n\n## Storing Credentials Safely with Export-Clixml\n\n`Export-Clixml` serializes a credential object to an XML file. The password is encrypted using the Windows Data Protection API (DPAPI), meaning **only the same user on the same computer** can decrypt it:\n\n```powershell\n# Save credentials to file\nGet-Credential | Export-Clixml -Path \"$HOME\\cred.xml\"\n\n# Load credentials later (no prompt needed)\n$cred = Import-Clixml -Path \"$HOME\\cred.xml\"\n```\n\nThis pattern is ideal for scheduled tasks and automation scripts that run unattended.\n\n## Using Credentials with Cmdlets\n\nMany cmdlets accept a `-Credential` parameter. Pass the `PSCredential` object directly:\n\n```powershell\n$cred = Import-Clixml -Path \"$HOME\\cred.xml\"\n\n# Remoting\nInvoke-Command -ComputerName Server01 -Credential $cred -ScriptBlock { hostname }\n\n# File operations on network shares\nNew-PSDrive -Name S -PSProvider FileSystem -Root '\\\\Server\\Share' -Credential $cred\n```\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\nNever store passwords as plain text in your scripts:\n\n```powershell\n# WRONG - password visible in source code\n$password = 'P@ssw0rd123'\n\n# WRONG - password visible in script file\n$cred = New-Object PSCredential('admin', (ConvertTo-SecureString 'P@ssw0rd123' -AsPlainText -Force))\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** If someone can read your script, they can read any plain-text password in it. Use `Export-Clixml`/`Import-Clixml`, Azure Key Vault, or the `SecretManagement` module instead.\n4:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"Intermediate PowerShell\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate/pssessions-and-remoting\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"PSSessions and Remoting\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[6,\" / \",6]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"h-8 w-8\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Credentials and SecureStrings\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Credentials and SecureStrings\",\"description\":\"Working with credentials safely.\",\"slug\":\"credentials-and-securestrings\",\"order\":6,\"prerequisites\":[\"m2-l5\"]},\"content\":\"$11\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m2-l6-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a command that prompts for credentials with a username of 'CONTOSO\\\\Admin' and stores the result in $cred.\",\"hints\":[\"Use Get-Credential with the -UserName parameter.\",\"Store the result in the $cred variable.\",\"Try: $cred = Get-Credential -UserName 'CONTOSO\\\\Admin'\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$cred\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Store the credential in a variable called $cred.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Credential\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-Credential to prompt for the password.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"CONTOSO\\\\\\\\Admin\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Specify the username as 'CONTOSO\\\\Admin'.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$cred = Get-Credential -UserName 'CONTOSO\\\\Admin'\",\"explanation\":\"Get-Credential with -UserName pre-fills the username and only prompts for the password. The result is a PSCredential object stored in $cred.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l6-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write commands that save a credential to a file using Export-Clixml, then load it back with Import-Clixml. Use the path '$HOME\\\\mycred.xml'.\",\"hints\":[\"First get the credential with Get-Credential and pipe to Export-Clixml.\",\"Then use Import-Clixml to read it back.\",\"Use -Path to specify the file location.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Credential\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-Credential to create the credential.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Export-Clixml\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Export-Clixml to save the credential to a file.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Import-Clixml\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Import-Clixml to load the credential from the file.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"mycred\\\\.xml\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the file path $HOME\\\\mycred.xml.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-Credential | Export-Clixml -Path \\\"$HOME\\\\mycred.xml\\\"\\n$cred = Import-Clixml -Path \\\"$HOME\\\\mycred.xml\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"Export-Clixml serializes the PSCredential object to XML with the password encrypted via DPAPI. Import-Clixml deserializes it back. Only the same user on the same machine can decrypt it.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l6-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a command that creates a PSCredential object manually from a $username variable and a SecureString $securePass variable using [PSCredential]::new().\",\"hints\":[\"Use [PSCredential]::new() with two arguments.\",\"The first argument is the username string.\",\"The second argument is the SecureString password.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"[PSCredential]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the [PSCredential] type.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"::new\\\\(\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use ::new() to call the constructor.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$username\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pass $username as the first argument.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$securePass\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pass $securePass as the second argument.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$cred = [PSCredential]::new($username, $securePass)\",\"explanation\":\"The PSCredential constructor takes a username string and a SecureString password. This is useful when you already have the components from other sources like Read-Host -AsSecureString.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l6-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a command that uses Read-Host to prompt for a password and store it as a SecureString in a variable called $securePass.\",\"hints\":[\"Use Read-Host with the -AsSecureString switch.\",\"The -Prompt parameter specifies the message shown to the user.\",\"Store the result in $securePass.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$securePass\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Store the result in $securePass.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Read-Host\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Read-Host to get input from the user.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-AsSecureString\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -AsSecureString to mask the input and store it securely.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$securePass = Read-Host -Prompt 'Enter password' -AsSecureString\",\"explanation\":\"Read-Host with -AsSecureString masks the user's input (showing asterisks) and returns a SecureString object instead of a plain-text string.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l6-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a command that uses Invoke-Command to run 'Get-Process' on 'Server01' using a credential loaded from '$HOME\\\\cred.xml' with Import-Clixml.\",\"hints\":[\"First load the credential with Import-Clixml.\",\"Then use Invoke-Command with -Credential.\",\"The -ScriptBlock should contain { Get-Process }.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Import-Clixml\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Import-Clixml to load the saved credential.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Invoke-Command\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Invoke-Command to run the remote command.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-Credential\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pass the credential with -Credential.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Process\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Run Get-Process in the script block.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Server01\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Target the computer Server01.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$cred = Import-Clixml -Path \\\"$HOME\\\\cred.xml\\\"\\nInvoke-Command -ComputerName Server01 -Credential $cred -ScriptBlock { Get-Process }\",\"explanation\":\"Import-Clixml loads the encrypted credential from disk. The PSCredential object is passed to Invoke-Command via -Credential, authenticating against the remote machine without prompting.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"intermediate\"}}],\"$L12\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate/pssessions-and-remoting\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"PSSessions and Remoting\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{}]]}]}]\na:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n13:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xl